{"text": "As a Senior ML Engineer with 8 years of experience, I specialize in deploying and optimizing deep learning models at scale. At NexusFast, I built a GPU-efficient model serving platform using Triton and CUDA, achieving 41% reduction in inference costs. I leveraged PyTorch with quantization-aware training, shrinking model sizes by 60% without accuracy loss. At GammaX, I developed a real-time feature store for incident prediction models, cutting data retrieval latency by 23%. I deployed transformer models with Weaviate-backed vector search, enabling semantic routing of 10K+ daily alerts. I also contributed to open-source integrations between LangChain and Weaviate for retrieval-augmented generation. At TerraEngine, I enhanced MLflow with custom serving backends, accelerating deployment cycles by 67%. My expertise spans full ML lifecycle with emphasis on low-latency serving and scalable feature management.\n\n• Used Triton for dynamic model batching and ensemble inference\n• Built feature stores syncing 500+ real-time features per second\n• Integrated Weaviate for vector similarity search in NLP pipelines\n• Deployed PyTorch models with CUDA kernels for E2E acceleration\n• Implemented Model Serving solutions handling 15K QPS\nSkills: Triton, CUDA, PyTorch, Model Serving, Weaviate, Feature Stores, LangChain, Vector DBs, Quantization", "domain": "ml_engineering", "seniority": "Senior", "years_experience": 8, "skills": ["Triton", "CUDA", "Model Serving", "PyTorch", "Weaviate", "Feature Stores", "LangChain", "Vector DBs", "Quantization"], "resume_type": "strong"}
{"text": "With 6 years of experience in machine learning engineering, I’ve focused on production-grade model deployment and infrastructure. At IonWorks, I designed a low-latency model serving system using Triton Inference Server, reducing inference time by 67%. By optimizing CUDA kernels for PyTorch models, I improved throughput on edge GPUs by 23%. I built a feature store supporting real-time threat detection, ingesting 2M events/sec with sub-50ms latency. At ShiftRapid, I integrated Weaviate as the vector database for user behavior search, increasing retrieval accuracy by 41%. I also implemented a BentoML-based CI/CD pipeline, cutting release cycles from days to hours. My work included serving LLMs with dynamic batching and embedding models for semantic indexing. I led cross-team efforts to standardize feature sharing and metadata tracking across 30+ ML applications. I have hands-on experience with both PyTorch and TensorFlow, with a strong emphasis on scalable serving and data pipeline integrity.\n\n• Deployed PyTorch models on Triton with multi-GPU support\n• Engineered CUDA custom ops for preprocessing acceleration\n• Scaled Weaviate cluster to handle 500K+ daily vector queries\n• Implemented Feature Stores with point-in-time correctness\n• Reduced model deployment time using BentoML and Kubernetes\nSkills: PyTorch, Triton, CUDA, Model Serving, Weaviate, Feature Stores, TensorFlow, BentoML, Vector DBs", "domain": "ml_engineering", "seniority": "Senior", "years_experience": 6, "skills": ["PyTorch", "Triton", "CUDA", "Model Serving", "Weaviate", "Feature Stores", "TensorFlow", "BentoML", "Vector DBs"], "resume_type": "strong"}
{"text": "Senior ML Engineer with 9 years of experience driving scalable ML infrastructure at high-growth tech firms. At FalconSwift, I architected a model serving platform using Triton and PyTorch, reducing p99 latency by 67% through CUDA kernel optimization. I led the development of a feature store unifying design behavior data, adopted by 80% of ML teams and cutting feature engineering time by 41%. At ZettaWeb, I deployed anomaly detection models using Weaviate for vector similarity search, improving incident clustering accuracy by 23%. I also integrated Pinecone as a secondary vector DB for A/B testing retrieval pipelines. Using quantization techniques (INT8, FP16), I reduced model footprint by 55%, enabling edge deployment. I built reusable BentoML bundles for model versioning and rollback, slashing deployment errors by 70%. My work bridges ML research and systems engineering, ensuring models are performant, observable, and maintainable in production.\n\n• Scaled Triton-based serving to handle 5K RPS\n• Optimized CUDA kernels for PyTorch inference\n• Deployed models with Model Serving pipelines on Kubernetes\n• Implemented Feature Stores with real-time stream ingestion\n• Leveraged Weaviate for semantic search in logs and events\nSkills: Model Serving, Triton, CUDA, PyTorch, Weaviate, Feature Stores, Quantization, Pinecone, BentoML", "domain": "ml_engineering", "seniority": "Senior", "years_experience": 9, "skills": ["Model Serving", "Triton", "CUDA", "PyTorch", "Weaviate", "Feature Stores", "Quantization", "Pinecone", "BentoML"], "resume_type": "strong"}
