{"text": "I'm a frontend engineer with 4 years of experience focused on accessibility, maintainable code, and developer tooling. I thrive in collaborative environments where clean UI and inclusive design are prioritized.\n\nAt NovaView (2020–2023), I led the integration of Storybook into our component workflow, increasing test coverage by 45% and adoption across 5 teams. I refactored core modules using modern JavaScript, improving bundle parse time by 31%. I also conducted WCAG 2.1 audits that resolved 90% of AA compliance issues in the dashboard.\n\nBefore that, I worked at XenonX (2018–2020), where I maintained large-scale Zustand stores and optimized Webpack builds to reduce CI/CD pipeline time by 23%. I mentored 3 junior developers and co-authored internal best practices for accessible React patterns.\n\nMy work consistently balances performance, accessibility, and team scalability. I rely heavily on Webpack for build optimization and JavaScript for scalable logic.", "domain": "frontend_engineering", "seniority": "Mid-level", "years_experience": 4, "skills": ["Webpack", "Storybook", "WCAG", "Zustand", "JavaScript"]}
{"text": "Frontend engineer with 6 years of experience specializing in performance optimization, CSS architecture, and modern build tools.\n\nSenior UI Engineer | Databricks | 2020–2023\n- Overhauled CSS delivery using Tailwind and purge strategies, reducing CSS bundle size by 67%.\n- Migrated Angular apps to Vite, cutting local rebuild times from 18s to 2.3s and improving developer velocity.\n- Led Web Performance initiative that improved Lighthouse scores from 52 to 91 across core dashboards.\n- Implemented Redux for global state, improving data consistency in multi-tab workflows.\n\nFrontend Developer | QuestTrust | 2017–2020\n- Built responsive incident management UIs with modular CSS, adopted by 12+ teams.\n- Upgraded Webpack configuration to support dynamic imports, reducing initial load by 41%.\n\nMy career has focused on making interfaces fast, maintainable, and scalable. I leverage Web Performance, CSS, Redux, Angular, Webpack, Vite, and Tailwind in production systems daily.", "domain": "frontend_engineering", "seniority": "Mid-level", "years_experience": 6, "skills": ["Web Performance", "CSS", "Redux", "Angular", "Webpack", "Vite", "Tailwind"]}
{"text": "I'm a frontend engineer with 3 years of experience building type-safe, testable applications using modern tooling. I focus on scalability and developer experience.\n\nFrontend Engineer | EdgeView | 2021–2023\n- Migrated codebase from JavaScript to TypeScript, improving code review efficiency by 38% and reducing runtime errors by 67%.\n- Integrated GraphQL with Apollo Client, reducing API payload sizes by 41% and improving caching efficiency.\n- Implemented Jest unit and integration tests across 15 core modules, increasing coverage from 54% to 89%.\n- Built UI components with Tailwind, accelerating feature delivery by 23%.\n\nEarlier, I contributed to internal design system at VectorWorks (2019–2021), where I used TypeScript and Jest to standardize component testing across teams.\n\nI'm passionate about strong typing, efficient styling, and robust testing. My core skills include TypeScript, GraphQL, Jest, and Tailwind—each proven in high-impact product environments.", "domain": "frontend_engineering", "seniority": "Mid-level", "years_experience": 3, "skills": ["TypeScript", "GraphQL", "Jest", "Tailwind"]}
{"text": "Mid-level frontend engineer with 5 years of experience building accessible, modular UIs for enterprise platforms.\n\nUI Engineer | TierSecure | 2020–2023\n- Developed 18 reusable Web Components adopted across 6 products, reducing UI duplication by 67%.\n- Enforced WCAG 2.1 standards across admin panels, achieving 98% compliance and passing accessibility audits.\n- Integrated Redux with middleware for analytics, improving event tracking accuracy by 41%.\n- Migrated legacy build system to Webpack 5 with module federation, cutting build time by 23%.\n- Styled components using Tailwind, enabling faster theming and responsive design.\n\nFrontend Developer | DataIndex | 2018–2020\n- Collaborated on design tool integrations, using Web Components and Tailwind for consistency.\n- Contributed to accessibility improvements that boosted screen reader compatibility by 58%.\n\nI specialize in Webpack, WCAG, Web Components, Tailwind, Redux, and Jest—applied to solve real-world scalability and inclusivity challenges.", "domain": "frontend_engineering", "seniority": "Mid-level", "years_experience": 5, "skills": ["Webpack", "WCAG", "Web Components", "Tailwind", "Redux", "Jest"]}
